></svg></div>Hint</div></div><div><div class=3D"flex flex-col" style=3D"pos=
ition: relative;"><div class=3D"HTMLContent_html__0OZLp" data-qd-rendered-d=
escription=3D"" data-track-load=3D"description_content"><p>Design a stack t=
hat supports push, pop, top, and retrieving the minimum element in constant=
 time.</p>

<p>Implement the <code>MinStack</code> class:</p>

<ul>
	<li><code>MinStack()</code> initializes the stack object.</li>
	<li><code>void push(int value)</code> pushes the element <code>value</code=
> onto the stack.</li>
	<li><code>void pop()</code> removes the element on the top of the stack.</=
li>
	<li><code>int top()</code> gets the top element of the stack.</li>
	<li><code>int getMin()</code> retrieves the minimum element in the stack.<=
/li>
</ul>

<p>You must implement a solution with <code>O(1)</code> time complexity for=
 each function.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input</strong>
["MinStack","push","push","push","getMin","pop","top","getMin"]
[[],[-2],[0],[-3],[],[],[],[]]

<strong>Output</strong>
[null,null,null,null,-3,null,0,-2]

<strong>Explanation</strong>
MinStack minStack =3D new MinStack();
minStack.push(-2);
minStack.push(0);
minStack.push(-3);
minStack.getMin(); // return -3
minStack.pop();
minStack.top();    // return 0
minStack.getMin(); // return -2
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li><code>-2<sup>31</sup> &lt;=3D val &lt;=3D 2<sup>31</sup> - 1</code></l=
i>
	<li>Methods <code>pop</code>, <code>top</code> and <code>getMin</code> ope=
rations will always be called on <strong>non-empty</strong> stacks.</li>
	<li>At most <code>3 * 10<sup>4</sup></code> calls will be made to <code>pu=
sh</code>, <code>pop</code>, <code>top</code>, and <code>getMin</code>.</li=
>
</ul>
