ition: relative;"><div class=3D"markdown-content_markdown__cVmKc"><p>The tr=
ick here is to understand that, since it is a stack and we don't care about=
 indexes, we don't need to worry about sorting...<br>
Example, let's say we push the elements -2, 0, -1, in that order.<br>
As we see, the minimum value is -2, so, the trick is to notice that we can'=
t ever get to the element with value -2 unless we pop the stack two times. =
I was giving it too much thought and wasted an hour on this, as my thought =
of process was: "If we pop -2, how are we going to know that -1 is the next=
 minimum value?" Until I realized we don't need to do that, as -2 is the fi=
rst value we inserted, so in order for -1 to be the next minimum value is t=
o pop the stack until -2 stops existing, in which case -1 would have alread=
y stopped existing as well.</p></div><span style=3D"font-size: 0px; line-he=
